<xml xmlns="https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml"><variables><variable id="v_joy_y">joy_y</variable><variable id="v_player_speed">player_speed</variable><variable id="v_player_y">player_y</variable><variable id="v_ball_x">ball_x</variable><variable id="v_ai_y">ai_y</variable><variable id="v_ball_y">ball_y</variable><variable id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</variable><variable id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</variable><variable id="v_player_score">player_score</variable><variable id="v_ai_score">ai_score</variable></variables><block type="program_start" id="pong_start" x="70" y="50"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">PROGRAM START runs only once. Here we prepare the hardware and set the initial values of all variables. It&#39;s a good idea to separate one-time initialization from repeated game logic in PROGRAM LOOP.</comment><next><block type="oled_init" id="pong_oled_init"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" display_type="AUTO"></mutation><field name="DISPLAY_TYPE">AUTO</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">OLED display initialization 128&#215;64. The game does not draw directly on the display, but first composes the entire image into a framebuffer and at the end of the loop sends it to the OLED with the refresh block.</comment><value name="SDA_PIN"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0001"><field name="NUM">21</field></shadow></value><value name="SCL_PIN"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0002"><field name="NUM">22</field></shadow></value><next><block type="joystick_init" id="pong_joystick_init"><field name="joy_name">1</field><field name="rot">270</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Joystick 1 initialization. In Pong, we use the Y-axis because the player&#39;s paddle stands to the left and moves up and down. Pins can be customized according to a specific board.</comment><value name="vrx"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0003"><field name="NUM">13</field></shadow></value><value name="vry"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0004"><field name="NUM">14</field></shadow></value><value name="sw"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0005"><field name="NUM">15</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0007"><field name="VAR" id="v_joy_y">joy_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Default joystick value. Zero means center position.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0006"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0009"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_y">player_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Vertical position of the left player&#39;s paddle. The paddle is 18px high, therefore Y=23 starts approximately in the middle of the 64px display.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0008"><field name="NUM">23</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0011"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_speed">player_speed</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The speed of the player&#39;s paddle in pixels per pass through the loop. Positive value moves down, negative value moves up.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0010"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0013"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Vertical position of the right paddle controlled by the computer. It starts just like the player in the middle.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0012"><field name="NUM">23</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0015"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Initial X coordinates of the ball. The four-pixel ball starts almost right in the middle of the screen.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0014"><field name="NUM">62</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0017"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The starting Y coordinates of the ball.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0016"><field name="NUM">30</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0019"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Horizontal speed of the ball. +2 means movement to the right two pixels after passing the loop; a negative value means movement to the left.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0018"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0021"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Vertical speed of the ball. +1 means downward movement, -1 means upward movement.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0020"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0023"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_score">player_score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Player points. The player gets a point when the computer misses the ball and the ball leaves the right margin.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0022"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0025"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_score">ai_score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The number of computer points. The computer gains a point when the player passes the ball to the left.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0024"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block><block type="program_loop" id="pong_loop" x="700" y="50"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">LOOP IS the heart of the game. He constantly reads the joystick, updates the paddles and ball, resolves collisions, and finally renders a new slide. Once completed, the next pass will begin immediately.</comment><statement name="DO"><block type="variables_set" id="b0026"><field name="VAR" id="v_joy_y">joy_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The current joystick value is stored in the joy_y variable so that we can use it multiple times in this slide.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="get_joy_axis_ble" id="pong_get_joy_y"><field name="joy_name">1</field><field name="axis">Y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Read the current Y-axis deflection of the joystick. The value is approximately from -100 to +100. The greater the absolute deflection, the faster the paddle will move.</comment></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0040"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_speed">player_speed</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The resulting speed retains the joystick sign: the negative speed moves the paddle up, the positive down.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_round" id="b0039"><field name="OP">ROUND</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Rounding ensures movement in whole pixels, which is clear for a small monochrome display.</comment><value name="NUM"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0038"><field name="OP">DIVIDE</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The deflection of the joystick is divided by 25. The range of approximately -100…+100 is thus converted to about -4…+4 px per passage through the loop.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0036"><field name="VAR" id="v_joy_y">joy_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0037"><field name="NUM">25</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0048"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_y">player_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">We update the position of the player&#39;s paddle according to the calculated speed.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_constrain" id="b0045"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Limit 0…46 holds 18px high paddle inside 64px display: 46 + 18 = 64.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0044"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Relative control: player_speed is added to the current position of player_y. Thus, the joystick does not determine the position directly, but the speed of changing the position.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0042"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_y">player_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0043"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_speed">player_speed</field></block></value></block></value><value name="LOW"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0046"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="HIGH"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0047"><field name="NUM">46</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0078"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">A computer paddle uses a very simple “AI”: when the ball arrives at its half, it tries to follow its Y-coordinate.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0051"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">A simple AI responds only when the ball is on the right half of the display. Thanks to this, the computer is not perfectly accurate and the game remains playable.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0049"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0050"><field name="NUM">64</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0064"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The first part of a simple AI controller: it follows the ball downwards.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0056"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">If the ball is under the center of the computer paddle, the paddle will move one pixel down.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0052"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0055"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">ai_y + 10 represents the approximate center of an 18px high paddle.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0053"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0054"><field name="NUM">10</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0063"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Move the right paddle down one pixel.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_constrain" id="b0060"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Like the player&#39;s paddle, the AI must not leave the screen.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0059"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The AI moves only 1 px per pass, so it&#39;s not faster than everything else.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0057"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0058"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="LOW"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0061"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="HIGH"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0062"><field name="NUM">46</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0077"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The second part of the AI controller: follows the ball upwards.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0069"><field name="OP">LT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">If the ball is above the target area of the paddle, the AI will move up.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0065"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0068"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">ai_y + 6 is the point slightly above the centre of the paddle. A small AI dead zone is created between +6 and +10.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0066"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0067"><field name="NUM">6</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0076"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Move the right paddle up one pixel.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_constrain" id="b0073"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Restriction will prevent the paddle from moving over the top edge.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0072"><field name="OP">MINUS</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Subtract 1 px from the AI position, i.e. move the paddle up.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0070"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0071"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="LOW"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0074"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="HIGH"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0075"><field name="NUM">46</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></statement></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0082"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Update the X coordinates of the ball.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0081"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">New horizontal position of the ball = old position + horizontal speed.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0079"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0080"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0086"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Updating the Y coordinates of the ball.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0085"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">New vertical position of the ball = old position + vertical speed.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0083"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0084"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0096"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Collision with the upper edge. The ball returns to the playing area and reverses the vertical speed.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0095"><field name="OP">LT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Upper collision occurs when ball_y drops below 1.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0093"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0094"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0092"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Return the ball exactly to the upper safe coordinate Y=0 so that it does not stay behind the edge of the display.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0091"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0090"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the upper wall, turn the vertical direction of the ball.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0089"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Multiplying the speed -1 reverses its sign and thus the direction of movement.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0087"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0088"><field name="NUM">-1</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0106"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Collision with the lower edge of the display.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0105"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The bottom collision occurs when the top coordinate of the 4px ball exceeds Y=59.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0103"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0104"><field name="NUM">59</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0098"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Return the four-pixel ball to Y=59 so that it remains on the 64px display.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0097"><field name="NUM">59</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0102"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Reflection from the lower wall turns the ball upward.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0101"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Again, we just reverse the vertical velocity sign.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0099"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0100"><field name="NUM">-1</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0126"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The collision of the player&#39;s paddle is deliberately broken down into several simple conditions to show that the collision of the rectangles is a combination of tests on both axes.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0109"><field name="OP">LT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">First, we verify that the ball has reached the left paddle. The paddle starts at X=2 and is 3px wide.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0107"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0108"><field name="NUM">6</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0125"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The second part of the collision: we verify the vertical overlap of the ball with the paddle.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0114"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The ball must not be completely above the player&#39;s paddle.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0110"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0113"><field name="OP">MINUS</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">player_y - 4 also counts the height of the ball so that the overlap of both rectangles works.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0111"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_y">player_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0112"><field name="NUM">4</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0124"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The third part of the collision: the ball is above the bottom edge of the paddle. If all three tests are valid, the paddle will deflect the ball.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0119"><field name="OP">LT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The ball must not be below the bottom edge of the player&#39;s paddle.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0115"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0118"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">player_y + 18 is the bottom edge of the paddle.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0116"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_y">player_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0117"><field name="NUM">18</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0121"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting, move the ball just in front of the paddle. This will prevent repeated rebound in several consecutive loops.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0120"><field name="NUM">5</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0123"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the left paddle, the ball must fly to the right, so we set a positive horizontal speed of +2.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0122"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement></block></statement></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0146"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The right paddle collision uses the same algorithm as the left one. This is a good example of a recurring pattern that could be moved to a function in a larger project.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0129"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The right paddle starts at X=123. A four-pixel ball touches it approximately from ball_x &gt; 118.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0127"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0128"><field name="NUM">118</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0145"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The second part of the collision with the right paddle: vertical overlap.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0134"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The ball must not be all over the right paddle.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0130"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0133"><field name="OP">MINUS</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The same overlapping principle as the player&#39;s paddle: we count the height of the ball.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0131"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0132"><field name="NUM">4</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0144"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The third part of the collision with the right paddle.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0139"><field name="OP">LT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The ball must not be under the right paddle.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0135"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0138"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The bottom edge of the right paddle is ai_y + 18.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0136"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0137"><field name="NUM">18</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0141"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting, set the ball just in front of the right paddle.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0140"><field name="NUM">119</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0143"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the right paddle, set the negative speed -2, so the ball flies back to the left.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0142"><field name="NUM">-2</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement></block></statement></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0162"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Point detection for the computer and preparation of a new submission.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0161"><field name="OP">LT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">If ball_x drops below 0, the ball has left the screen to the left and has not been bounced by the player.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0159"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0160"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0150"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_score">ai_score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The player misses the ball, so the computer gets the point.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0149"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">We add one point to the computer score.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0147"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_score">ai_score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0148"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0152"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After the point, return the ball to the center of the screen.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0151"><field name="NUM">62</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0154"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">We also return its Y-coordinate to the center.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0153"><field name="NUM">30</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0156"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After the computer point, we will send a new ball to the right.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0155"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0158"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The new submission will start with a slight downward movement.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0157"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0178"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Point detection for the player and preparation of the next submission.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0177"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">If ball_x exceeds 124, the entire four-pixel ball has already left the right side of the display.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0175"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0176"><field name="NUM">124</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0166"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_score">player_score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The computer missed the ball, so the player gets the point.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0165"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">We add one point to the player&#39;s score.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0163"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_score">player_score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0164"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0168"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After the point, return the ball to the middle.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0167"><field name="NUM">62</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0170"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The Y-coordinate of the new submission is again in the middle.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0169"><field name="NUM">30</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0172"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After the player point, we will send a new submission to the left.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0171"><field name="NUM">-2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0174"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">This time, the new submission will start with a slight upward movement.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0173"><field name="NUM">-1</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0190"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">A simple rule of the game: play up to five points. After the fifth point, the score is automatically reset.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_operation" id="b0185"><field name="OP">OR</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Logical OR: We will start a new match if five points are scored by either side.</comment><value name="A"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0181"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The player won the match if he scored at least 5 points.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0179"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_score">player_score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0180"><field name="NUM">4</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="B"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0184"><field name="OP">GT</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The computer won the match if it scored at least 5 points.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0182"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_score">ai_score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0183"><field name="NUM">4</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0187"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_score">player_score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">At the end of the match, we will reset the player&#39;s score.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0186"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0189"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_score">ai_score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">We will also reset the computer score and the next pass belongs to the new match.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0188"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="fb_fill" id="pong_fb_clear"><field name="barva">0</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">At the beginning of the rendering, delete the entire framebuffer with color 0. In each frame, we draw the game scene again and there are no traces of moving objects.</comment><next><block type="fb_draw_pic" id="QcQ/Mvl%RETEz9#H69bh"><field name="name">Pong_ball_4x4</field><field name="alpha">-1</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The ball is a 4&#215;4px bitmap. We draw it in front of the paddles, because the bitmap does not have transparency; if the ball with the paddle overlaps, then the drawn paddle will remain visually on top.</comment><value name="px"><block type="variables_get" id="s~YU.b;q5YV{a0?97ru8"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="py"><block type="variables_get" id="j;CR#R5=k!fW,PyGR,=u"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="data"><shadow type="text" id=":oT6g7a)tYhkpXig2i5("><field name="TEXT">bytearray(b'\x06\x0f\x0f\x06'), 4, 8</field></shadow></value><next><block type="fb_rect_fill" id="pong_center_line"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The center line visually divides half the player and the computer. It is drawn before the ball, so the ball will cover it properly when passing through.</comment><value name="px"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0191"><field name="NUM">63</field></shadow></value><value name="py"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0192"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="sirka"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0193"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><value name="vyska"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0194"><field name="NUM">64</field></shadow></value><value name="col"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0195"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type="fb_rect_fill" id="pong_player_score_bar"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The player&#39;s score is displayed in a simple bar to the left of the center. It is intentionally without text, so that the project uses only basic graphic blocks.</comment><value name="px"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0199"><field name="NUM">50</field></shadow></value><value name="py"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0200"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><value name="sirka"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0198"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Each player point increases the score indicator by 2 pixels.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0196"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_score">player_score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0197"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="vyska"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0201"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><value name="col"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0202"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type="fb_rect_fill" id="pong_ai_score_bar"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The top right bar represents the computer score. The match will automatically restart after five points.</comment><value name="px"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0206"><field name="NUM">68</field></shadow></value><value name="py"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0207"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><value name="sirka"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0205"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Each point of the computer increases the right pointer by 2 pixels.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0203"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_score">ai_score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0204"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="vyska"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0208"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><value name="col"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0209"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type="fb_rect_fill" id="pong_player_paddle_draw"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Player&#39;s paddle: filled rectangle 3&#215;18 px on the left edge. Its Y-coordinates are created by relative joystick control.</comment><value name="px"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0214"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><value name="py"><block type="variables_get" id="b0213"><field name="VAR" id="v_player_y">player_y</field></block></value><value name="sirka"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0215"><field name="NUM">3</field></shadow></value><value name="vyska"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0216"><field name="NUM">18</field></shadow></value><value name="col"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0217"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type="fb_rect_fill" id="pong_ai_paddle_draw"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Computer paddle: same rectangle on the right side. Its position is changed by a simple AI according to the ball.</comment><value name="px"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0219"><field name="NUM">123</field></shadow></value><value name="py"><block type="variables_get" id="b0218"><field name="VAR" id="v_ai_y">ai_y</field></block></value><value name="sirka"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0220"><field name="NUM">3</field></shadow></value><value name="vyska"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0221"><field name="NUM">18</field></shadow></value><value name="col"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0222"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type="oded_refresh" id="pong_refresh"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Only now will we send the complete framebuffer to OLED. The separation of &quot;game calculation&quot; and &quot;frame rendering&quot; is an important principle used even in large games.</comment></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block>
  <!--ESPIDE_EXTENSIONS_BEGIN-->
eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJwcm9jZXNzb3IiOiJTaW11bGF0b3IiLCJleHRlbnNpb25zIjpbXX0=
<!--ESPIDE_EXTENSIONS_END-->
</xml>
